     1	# Production deployment
     2	
     3	For the global-control/regional-cell ownership model, routing assertions,
     4	failure behavior, workspace moves, outages, and key rotation, see
     5	[`global-control-plane.md`](./global-control-plane.md). The topology manifest
     6	must be validated and every private cell deployed before enabling gateway mode.
     7	
     8	The checked-in transition deployment still deploys the single-cell Skillplane
     9	app and MCP Workers backed by one PostgreSQL database and one private R2 bucket.
    10	The multi-cell renderer in `scripts/lib/topology-deployment.mjs` generates the
    11	next-stage canonical app/MCP gateways plus private app/MCP workers for every
    12	cell in `deployment/topology.production.json`. It requires separate control and
    13	cell Hyperdrive IDs and separate public/regional bucket names. Generated cell
    14	workers have no route, no `workers.dev` exposure, no downstream service
    15	bindings, and no Email Service binding. Promotion of those generated configs is
    16	an explicit rollout step after the cells and projection drainer are provisioned;
    17	it is not an automatic side effect of the legacy `deploy:all` command.
    18	
    19	The
    20	landing Worker is maintained and deployed independently from the 21n monorepo's
    21	`landing/skillplane` workspace. The production hosts are
    22	`skillplane.dev`, `app.skillplane.dev`, `mcp.skillplane.dev`, and the PostHog
    23	reverse proxy at `user.skillplane.dev`.
    24	
    25	## One-time provider preparation
    26	
    27	Before the first release:
    28	
    29	1. Create a password-authenticated production PostgreSQL database reachable over
    30	   TLS, enable the provider's managed backup and point-in-time recovery policy,
    31	   and retain its direct URL for migration and backup processes only.
    32	2. Create a Cloudflare Hyperdrive configuration whose origin is that PostgreSQL
    33	   database. Record its 32-character ID. Do not put the direct database URL into
    34	   a Worker variable.
    35	3. Create a production Turnstile widget restricted to
    36	   `app.skillplane.dev`. Record its site key and secret key.
    37	4. Complete Cloudflare Email Service onboarding for `skillplane.dev`, including
    38	   the sender `no-reply@auth.skillplane.dev`, and confirm arbitrary-recipient
    39	   transactional sending is enabled.
    40	5. Create the PostHog managed reverse proxy for `user.skillplane.dev` by
    41	   following the [PostHog reverse-proxy guide](https://posthog.com/docs/advanced/proxy).
    42	   Point an unproxied DNS-only CNAME at the PostHog-provided proxy target and
    43	   wait until PostHog reports the proxy as live.
    44	6. Confirm the Wrangler identity has Workers Scripts, Workers Routes,
    45	   Hyperdrive read, R2 read/write, and Email Sending permissions. The zone must
    46	   be active in the same Cloudflare account.
    47	
    48	`pnpm deploy:all` creates `skillplane-skill-bundles` only when it is absent. If
    49	the bucket has no lifecycle action, it adds only a seven-day incomplete
    50	multipart upload abort rule. It then refuses deployment if the bucket has an
    51	object-expiration or storage transition rule, an enabled `r2.dev` URL, or a
    52	custom domain. Published skill bundles never receive age-based deletion.
